        ":question/worked-solution": "First, we express $f(x)$ as the composite function\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\log_{9}(u),\\quad u=4 x - 9.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}f}{\\mathrm{d}u}=\\frac{1}{u\\ln(9)},\\quad \\frac{\\mathrm{d}u}{\\mathrm{d}x}=4.\n$$\n\nWe now apply the chain rule, and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\mathrm{d}f}{\\mathrm{d}x} &=\\frac{\\mathrm{d}f}{\\mathrm{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\mathrm{d}u}{\\mathrm{d}x}\\\\ &=\\frac{1}{u\\ln(9)}\\cdot (4)\\\\ &=\\frac{1}{(4 x - 9)\\ln(9)}\\cdot (4)\\\\ &=\\frac{4}{4 x - 9}\\frac{1}{\\ln(9)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
