        ":question/worked-solution": "First, we express $y$ as the composite function\n\n$$\ny=\\log_{9}(u),\\quad u=\\sqrt{7 x}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}u}=\\frac{1}{u\\ln(9)},\\quad \\frac{\\mathrm{d}u}{\\mathrm{d}x}=\\frac{7}{2\\sqrt{7 x}}.\n$$\n\nWe now apply the chain rule, and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x} &=\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\mathrm{d}u}{\\mathrm{d}x}\\\\ &=\\frac{1}{u\\ln(9)}\\cdot (\\frac{7}{2\\sqrt{7 x}})\\\\ &=\\frac{1}{(\\sqrt{7 x})\\ln(9)}\\cdot (\\frac{7}{2\\sqrt{7 x}})\\\\ &=\\frac{7}{2(7 x)\\ln(9)}\\\\ &=\\frac{\\cancel{7}}{2\\cdot \\cancel{7}x\\ln(9)}\\\\ &=\\frac{1}{2 x \\ln{(9 )}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
